.TH geectl-pull-request-decline 1  "geectl-pull-request-decline 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-pull\-request\-decline \- Decline a pull request. On OBS this changes the request state to declined; on Gitea it closes the pull request. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl pull\-request decline\fR [\fB\-\-message\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREFERENCE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Decline a pull request. On OBS this changes the request state to declined; on Gitea it closes the pull request. Dry\-run by default; mutates only with `\-\-live`
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-message\fR \fI<MESSAGE>\fR
The reason for the decline or withdrawal. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a message may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREFERENCE\fR>
The pull\-request handle: `obs:<id>` or `gitea:<owner>/<repo>#<number>`
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
